{
  "number": 3494,
  "title": "[BUG] context_offloader FileStorage: sandbox-bound retrieve() rejects the bare filenames its docstring promises",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/3494",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-07-27T15:02:01Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-07-27T18:49:48Z",
  "body": "### Checks\n\n- [x] I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands\n- [x] I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior\n- [x] I have searched [./issues](./issues?q=) and there are no duplicates of my issue\n\n### SDK Language\n\nPython\n\n### Strands Version\n\n1.50.1\n\n### Language Runtime Version\n\nPython 3.13\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS 26.5, also seen on a deployed Bedrock AgentCore runtime\n\n### Installation Method\n\npip (uv)\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n```py\nimport asyncio\nimport tempfile\n\nfrom strands.sandbox.not_a_sandbox_local_environment import NotASandboxLocalEnvironment\nfrom strands.vended_plugins.context_offloader import FileStorage\n\n\nasync def main() -> None:\n    host = FileStorage(tempfile.mkdtemp())\n    reference = await host.store(\"tooluse_abc123_0\", b\"payload\", \"text/plain\")\n    print(\"store() ->\", reference)\n    try:\n        await host.retrieve(reference.split(\"/\")[-1].removesuffix(\".txt\"))\n    except KeyError as error:\n        print(\"host, no extension ->\", error)\n\n    sandboxed = host.for_sandbox(NotASandboxLocalEnvironment())\n    sandbox_reference = await sandboxed.store(\"tooluse_abc123_1\", b\"payload\", \"text/plain\")\n    print(\"sandboxed, full path ->\", (await sandboxed.retrieve(sandbox_reference))[1])\n    try:\n        await sandboxed.retrieve(sandbox_reference.split(\"/\")[-1])\n    except KeyError as error:\n        print(\"sandboxed, bare filename ->\", error)\n\n\nasyncio.run(main())\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\n`retrieve()` accepts what its docstring promises (`strands/vended_plugins/context_offloader/storage.py:220-221`):\n\n> Accepts both full paths (as returned by `store()`) and bare filenames for backward compatibility.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nstore() -> /var/folders/.../1785164954198_1_tooluse_abc123_0.txt\nhost, no extension -> 'Reference not found: 1785164954198_1_tooluse_abc123_0'\nsandboxed, full path -> text/plain\nsandboxed, bare filename -> 'Reference not found: 1785164954200_1_tooluse_abc123_1.txt'\n```\n\nTwo gaps:\n\n1. The sandbox-bound branch accepts no bare filename at all, since `storage.py:234-236` requires the `artifact_dir/` prefix.\n2. Neither branch accepts the stem without the extension `store()` chose (`storage.py:165-169`).\n\nUnder an `Agent` only the sandbox branch runs: `Agent.sandbox` is never `None` (`agent/agent.py:299`) and `_storage_for_agent` binds file storage through `for_sandbox` when the plugin is registered (`strands/plugins/registry.py:92`, `plugin.py:263-268`), so the full path is the only accepted form.\n\n### Additional Context\n\nThe retrieval tool documents references as `\"ref_1\"` and `\"mem_1_tool-123_0\"` (`strands/vended_plugins/context_offloader/plugin.py:328-334`), which is `InMemoryStorage`'s scheme, while `FileStorage` emits absolute paths. Models send the stem and lose a round trip. In production the agent sent the stem, got not-found, then retried with the full path.\n\n`strands.storage.LocalFileStorage` is symmetric (the reference is the bare key it accepts), so if the legacy backend is being retired, a deprecation plus a docstring fix resolves this too.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nNormalize in `retrieve()`, in both branches: take the basename, and when it carries no extension match it by stem against the known `_content_types` keys.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n#3110, #3476, #3493\n\n\n\n",
